"""Build Golden A v2 (RAG) for the Saral borrower assistant and verify every anchor.

    python scripts/golden/build_rag_v2.py --chunks <dir with saral_nbfc_policy.chunks.jsonl and rbi_regulatory.chunks.jsonl>

Every item below was written and checked by hand (origin "frontier-authored"); none was generated by a small or local
model. Each answerable item is anchored to verbatim quotes (whitespace-normalised) inside named chunks of the corpus v3
collections. The build stops if any quote is not found in its chunk. Without --chunks the build still runs, but it can
only check chunk ids and chunk hashes against data/corpus_v3/chunk_index.csv (the chunk texts are not committed).

The schema keeps every saral_golden_v1 field (qid, category, topic, collection, language, question, turns,
expected_behavior, expected_answer, anchors, conflict, note, origin, review_status, gold_docs, gold_chunks,
conflict_note, calibration, golden_version) so v1 tooling still reads it. v2 adds: variant, script, behaviour_kind,
must_include, must_not_include, difficulty, source_url, v1_qid, collections, split.

expected_behavior:
  answer       answer from the cited policy text
  answer_note  answer, cite the figure with its source, and note the recorded discrepancy (conflicts C1-C8)
  clarify      ask a clarifying question before a personalised answer (general facts may be given)
  abstain      say the information is not in Saral's sources (other lenders, internal criteria, unknown internals)
  refuse       decline (out of scope, prompt injection, approval promise, record tampering, coaching to game checks)
"""
